[0.456, "o", "\u001b[2mpotsherd find \"pgbouncer\" · 2 sessions · bm25 · 14ms\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  Pool PostgreSQL connections through pgbouncer                    \u001b[2mclaude · live\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2mdata-pipeline · 21 aug · 8 exchanges · main\u001b[0m                             \u001b[2m0.0275\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2mPool PostgreSQL connections through \u001b[0m\u001b[38;5;209mpgbouncer\u001b[0m\u001b[2m\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2mput \u001b[0m\u001b[38;5;209mpgbouncer\u001b[0m\u001b[2m in front of it in transaction pooling mode\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2mrun  claude --resume 9c4d2f18-7a3b-4e05-b6d1-0f2a58e17c43\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  Move payments-api onto pgbouncer                                \u001b[38;5;209mclaude · ghost\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2mpayments-api · 13 nov 2025 · 241 prompts recovered · main\u001b[0m               \u001b[2m0.0184\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m…prepared statements are failing behind \u001b[0m\u001b[38;5;209mpgbouncer\u001b[0m\u001b[2m — what are the options?\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2mcompare \u001b[0m\u001b[38;5;209mpgbouncer\u001b[0m\u001b[2m session pooling against transaction pooling for a worker…\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2massistant side not recoverable · potsherd show 77c6a3a4\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[2m1 ghost hit\u001b"]
