[0.024, "o", "\u001b[2mpotsherd ask \"what did we decide about prepared statements behind the pooler?\"\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nANSWER\r\n  We decided to set statement_cache_size=0 so the client stops preparing\r\n  statements client-side. \u001b[38;5;209m[1]\u001b[0m This was verified to fix the issue:\r\n  the old config failed with a \"prepared statement already exists\" error, while\r\n  disabling the cache passed. \u001b[38;5;209m[2]\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nEVIDENCE\r\n  [1] data-pipeline/9c4d2f18  21 aug 09:31  \u001b[2m\"the client has to stop preparing,…\"\u001b[0m\r\n  [2] data-pipeline/9c4d2f18  21 aug 09:42  \u001b[2m\"The test fails against the old cl…\"\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nOPEN THREADS\r\n  \u001b[38;5;214mpossible open thread\u001b[0m · decided in event-bus, not seen in data-pi…\r\n      Configure consumers to connect to connection pooler on 6432 instead of\r\n      postgres on 5432\r\n      \u001b[2mevent-bus/b2181bfe@1,2  11 aug 11:38\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;214mpossible open thread\u001b[0m · decided in data-pipeline, not seen in eve…\r\n      Deploy pgbouncer in transaction pooling mode\r\n      \u001b[2mdata-pipeline/9c4d2f18@2  21 aug 09:2"]
